//   - The internal state is protected by a single Mutex to maintain LRU order and TTL consistency.
//   - Entries store (value, expiry_time) where expiry_time is Option<Instant>.
//   - LRU order is maintained via a VecDeque of keys; most recently used at the back.
//   - On get, the key is moved to the back of the deque (most recently used).
//   - On insert, if capacity is exceeded, the least recently used (front) entry is evicted.
//   - TTL is checked on get; expired entries are treated as missing and removed lazily.
//   - Zero capacity means no entries can be stored; insert is a no-op, get always returns None.
//   - Negative capacity is not possible since usize is unsigned; capacity 0 is handled explicitly.
//   - Repeated close is not applicable here; cleanup happens on drop naturally.
//   - Loader/task failures are not part of this API; insert takes a value directly.
